    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. what about the sound though? sometimes when they're spooling up they make that really loud whistling or whining noise. is there a mechanical reason for that specific sound?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The loud whistling or whining noise when a turbocharger is spooling up is due to the rapid compression of the gas within the turbine, which creates a pressure wave that can be mistaken for a howling or whine sound. As the turbine shaft spins up, the gas quickly accelerates down the turbine nozzle, creating a shockwave that produces this characteristic noise. This noise typically occurs when the turbocharger is under boost pressure, around 10-20% of its maximum capacity, and can be more pronounced in cold temperatures or when the engine is not under high load.",
      "source": "target",
